# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
# /Training was removed when the embedded training UX shipped (v1.20.0):
# strip + DecksModal + SessionChevrons replace the standalone page so the
# user trains in-context on every page. Old inbound links and bookmarks
# land on home with no 404.
/Training/* / 301
/Training / 301

# Crackhead Control lived at a duplicate top-level path until v1.53.x; the
# canonical page is the Rubber Guard variant. Keep old inbound links working.
/Positions/Crackhead-Control/* /Positions/Rubber-Guard/Crackhead-Control/:splat 301
/Positions/Crackhead-Control /Positions/Rubber-Guard/Crackhead-Control 301

# Shareable technique lists (the gym-WhatsApp acquisition link, v1.81.x).
# A 200 is a REWRITE, not a redirect: /l/<code> keeps its URL in the browser (the app decodes
# the code from location.pathname) and serves the built static shell. This one line is what
# makes the feature work with NO Cloudflare Function deployed — if functions/l/[[path]].js is
# ever absent or fails to build, the recipient still gets the full focused experience and only
# the social link preview degrades to generic text. Asserted from the EMITTED _redirects by
# e2e/journeys/share-lists.spec.ts.
/l/* /l.html 200

# /Tree was a mount point for the interactive TreeExplorer, deleted with the rest of the
# legacy front-end in v1.80.0. The page's frontmatter sets hide-content, so what remains
# emits an empty <article> — a soft-404 waiting to be indexed. Deep navigation now lives in
# the Neural app's Explore tab, Search and the category hubs.
/Tree/* / 301
/Tree / 301

# v1.155.0 — the five twin-collapse deletions. Each of these was a live public URL with a hub
# page and Attacker/Defender role pages until the records were collapsed into their Submissions/
# twin (a move whose success edge reaches the game-over sink IS a submission and may not also
# exist as a transition record). regenerate_redirects.py walks the CURRENT content tree, so a
# DELETED page can never produce its own rule — these have to be hand-authored here or the URLs
# 404 and the inbound links rot. Splat first so /Attacker and /Defender land on their
# counterparts, then the exact hub rule.
/Transitions/Arm-Triangle-from-Turtle/* /Submissions/Arm-Triangle/from-Turtle/:splat 301
